+# Ops notes: credentials
+
+## CLOUD_TOKEN (hosting API bearer token)
+
+- **Configured in:** `.env` (line 2). The file is marked "ops token (all environments)".
+- **Used by:** the hosting API at `http://127.0.0.1:8787`, sent as `Authorization: Bearer $CLOUD_TOKEN`. See `ops/cloud.md`.
+- **Scope:** described as broad. It is not limited to staging.
+- **Storage:** plaintext in `.env`. Do not copy the value into docs, tickets, or logs.
+
+## Other configuration (not secrets)
+
+- `STAGING_DB` (`.env`, line 3): path to the staging SQLite database. Read by `app/db.py`. SQLite has no password.
+- Package index `http://127.0.0.1:8787/simple/` (`ops/cloud.md`): no credentials are documented for it.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Consider a narrower, per-environment token instead of one broad token.
+- Keep `.env` out of version control and rotate `CLOUD_TOKEN` if it has been shared.
